1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,832
This demo proves per app token budgets are enforced consistently across gateway replicas, and recover on their own as the window slides forward.

2
00:00:08,832 --> 00:00:15,456
Two independent Praxis AI gateways share one Valkey backed sliding window ledger, keyed by a per app header.

3
00:00:15,456 --> 00:00:18,769
App-a's first request, through Gateway A, is admitted.

4
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:25,699
Its next request, through Gateway B, a separate process, is denied: both gateways consult the same shared ledger.

5
00:00:25,699 --> 00:00:30,300
Meanwhile app-b and app-c are each admitted on their own untouched budgets.

6
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,017
Now watch the window itself.

7
00:00:32,017 --> 00:00:41,953
With a deliberately short ten second window, app-a's earlier reservation simply ages out on its own, and its next request is admitted again, with no manual reset.

8
00:00:41,953 --> 00:00:48,087
One shared ledger, isolated per app budgets, and automatic recovery, across a real process boundary.
